    {
      "title": "Default Argument Pitfalls",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Default Argument Pitfalls",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Evaluated Once",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Defaults are built ==once==, at `def` time",
                "Stored in `f.__defaults__`, reused on every call",
                "{green:Safe}: int, str, tuple, None",
                "{red:Danger}: a default that is mutated or reused"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Trap and the Fix",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`add(1)` then `add(2)` share ==one list==, giving `[1, 2]`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "def add(x, acc=[]):",
                "    acc.append(x)",
                "    return acc",
                "add(1); add(2)",
                "print(add.__defaults__)"
              ],
              "note": "the default list itself changed"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "([1, 2],)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Fix: `acc=None`, then `acc = [] if acc is None else acc`",
                "`time.time()` or `datetime.now()` as a default freezes at def time",
                "Compute it inside the body"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why does the list persist?** One list is made at `def` time and every call reuses it",
                "**How to inspect a default?** Read `f.__defaults__`",
                "**When is it intentional?** A memo cache, e.g. `def fib(n, memo={})`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
