              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`@dec` above `def f` is exactly ==f = dec(f)==",
                "Wrapper takes `*args, **kwargs`: fits any signature",
                "Add ==@functools.wraps(fn)== or `__name__` and `__doc__` are lost"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import functools",
                "def log(fn):",
                "    @functools.wraps(fn)",
                "    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):",
                "        return fn(*args, **kwargs)",
                "    return wrapper"
              ],
              "note": "standard template"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Decorator with Arguments",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "retry(3)",
                    "sub": "returns decorator",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "decorator(fn)",
                    "sub": "returns wrapper",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "wrapper(*a, **kw)",
                    "sub": "calls fn",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Timing decorator?** `time.perf_counter()` before and after `fn(...)`, then return the result",
                "**Why wraps?** Keeps `__name__` and `__doc__`",
                "**@retry(3)?** Expands to `f = retry(3)(f)`",
                "**Stacking?** Applied ==bottom-up==; the top decorator is outermost"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Three layers",
              "text": "Arguments add one outer function: ==factory → decorator → wrapper==."
            }
          ]
